  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN234.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ ṟērpākaṟkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE said to [his] charioteer.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN234.1">
        <l>kārpayam poḻinta nīrtikaḻ kālai</l>
        <l>nuṇṇayir paranta taṇṇaya maruṅki</l>
        <l>ṉirai<supplied>pa</supplied>ṟai yaṉṉat taṉṉa <supplied>vi</supplied>raiparip</l>
        <l>pulluḷaik kalimā mellitiṟ koḷīi</l>
        <l>va<supplied>ḷ</supplied>poruṅ kamaiyap paṟṟi muḷkiya</l>
        <l>palkati rāḻi melvaḻi yaṟuppak</l>
        <l>kāleṉa ma<supplied>ruḷa</supplied> vēṟi nūliyaṟ</l>
        <l>kaṇṇōk koḻikkum paṇṇamai neṭuntēr</l>
        <l>valvirain tūrti <supplied>na</supplied>lvalam peṟutti</l>
        <l>tātaḷai muṉaiiya teṟinaṭai maṭappiṇai</l>
        <l>peṟupuṇa ruvakaiya vūṟila vukaḷa</l>
        <l><anchor n="1"/>vañciṟai vaṇṭiṉ meṉpaṟait toḻuti</l>
        <l>mullai naṟumalart tātunayan tū<supplied>ta</supplied></l>
        <l>vellai pōkiya pulleṉ mālaip</l>
        <l>puṟavaṭain tirunta vuṟaivi ṉallūrk</l>
        <l>kaḻipaṭa ruḻanta paṉivā ruṇka</l>
        <l>ṇaṉṉiṟam pacanta pacalaiyaṇ</l>
        <l>miṉṉē rōtip piṉṉuppiṇi viṭavē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="9ab">Very speedily mount</l>
        <l corresp="8">the long chariot of a construction that avoids the look of the eye</l>
        <l corresp="7">following the treatise, rising [fast] like the wind,</l>
        <l corresp="5d-6">while the many-spoked wheels that gouge [the ground] cut into the soft road,</l>
        <l corresp="5a-c">[you] aptly seizing the reins simultaneously</l>
        <l corresp="4">gently holding back the spirited horses with tawny manes,</l>
        <l corresp="3">as fast in motion as geese flying in an order,</l>
        <l corresp="2">by the side of the cool water that spreads through the fine sand,</l>
        <l corresp="1">at the time glittering with water that flowed from the monsoon’s yield,</l>
        <l corresp="18">− so that she lets go of the band that binds [her] sparkling fine hair,</l>
        <l corresp="17">the one [afflicted by] pallor into which [her] good complexion faded,</l>
        <l corresp="16">with kajal eyes flowing over with tears, who bore great distress</l>
        <l>in the good village pleasing to stay where, in the woodland,</l>
        <l corresp="14f">bleak evening has settled as the daylight is gone,</l>
        <l>when the soft-winged multitude of pretty-winged bees,</l>
        <l corresp="12f">keenly feed on the pollen of the fragrant jasmine blossoms,</l>
        <l>while the youthful does with leaping gait, who hated the pollen mixture,</l>
        <l>after having [re]gained good strength</l>
        <l corresp="9d-11">frolic without hindrance, overjoyed by the union they are having.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

